A||||12||Roy||Dream Swap ||||7||
Z||000000||Roy||05-26-2000||04:47 PM||||Today I finally sat down and was reading my july issue of kit car. There's a story in there about fords SHO v6. In this story they were putting it into a cobra replica. But the more I read about the engine the more I started thinking about how this engine would fair in our plastic bodied friends <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Stock the engine is rated at 220hp at 6500rpms, its a 3L engine, fuel injected. No idea on the torque on the engine, or the weight. But with a paxton supercharger this engine is rated at 346hp at 6500rpms. If anyone has any sites with information on this engine I'd love to have them. I'd really like to know the weight, torque and dimensions.<P>Roy||||reg||7
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||05-26-2000||05:06 PM||||I have a ford 4 banger turbo out of a turbo coupe t-bird that would be great for the fiero, but the problem is I don't know if there is a transverse tranny that you could use with it.  If I could find a tranny I just might try it some day!||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||05-26-2000||05:09 PM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.shotimes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shotimes.com</A> <BR>Yes, this is a killer engine.  High revving and very durable.  Its Chevy counterpart is the 24 valve 3.4L DOHC.  Some people on this board have done the 3.4l DOHC swap. Kits are available for this swap but probably not for the SHO swap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||05-26-2000||10:29 PM||||I did a little reasearch on that one,wanted to put one in my Lancia Scorpion,would use the transverse SHO trans I guess,too large for that car though.<BR>It would be alot easier in a Fiero to just use a 3.4TDC,as it bolts to the stock Fiero tranny,flywheel,clutch,uses stock motor mounts,axles,the electrics are compatible with all the stock guages...<BR>Twice the effort,if not more.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||05-27-2000||01:10 AM||||There was a company in California mentioned in one of the FOCOA magazines that was doing SHO swaps. I posted a message to the fiero list about a year ago and got the names of a couple places that do the swap. I can't remember the names of the places off hand, but try posting the fiero list abou the question and see if you can get the phone numbers from the guys there. I'll also look throuhg my old message archive when I get home and see if I get the name and numbers of the businesses for ya. Later||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||05-27-2000||01:28 AM||||If you want to consider outrageous engine swaps, consider this. My previous car was an Eagle Talon TSi, the best part of which was the engine. These 2.0L DOHC turbos are ridiculously easy to get 400 street driveable  horsepower out of. The cars they are in weigh from 3100-3300 lbs, and they are easily capable of running mid 12's with external mods only. A few guys I know run in the 11's with cars that are daily drivers. Now imagine, lighter and more compact than an iron duke, tough as an anvil and huge hp/cu. in potential. This one is still at the top of my list for a swap into my Fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||phillip||05-27-2000||06:05 AM||||turbo northstar with a strong enough mamual tranny is the dream swap for me.||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||05-27-2000||08:53 AM||||Was thinking that if I ever have to smog test my car,that a pair of turbos on the 3.4TDC would be the solution.Turbos are good for emissions,except in CA where they're so anal with inspections that they're counter-productive as far as smog goes; the car has to "look" stock,doesn't matter what comes out the pipe.<BR>Does anyone know what the North*s use for an exhaust system when put into a Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||05-28-2000||09:28 PM||||I have that same Kit Car, and it was exactly that article that got me thinking about a 3.4, TDC, or the new 3.5lt engine (215hp, bone stock) from the Olds Alero, with a Paxton or Vortech Supercharger. Have done only a little of the legwork....<P>The Getrag tranny was a question for me. Something similar was brought up in a post weeks ago, and the response that seems to fit is, it'll work well, but the question is, for how long. The answer to how long is how you treat it....<P>Of course, there are plenty of V8s hooked up to Porsche transaxles, which seems to me to be the only answer to a manual Northstar. All I know is I don't have that kind of money....||||reg||1
Z||000009||Guinea Pig||05-28-2000||09:59 PM||||Bob Steiger of Twin Lakes Fiero, Paxton, Il. is currently putting an SHO in a Fiero.  He will be at the Wisconsin Dells Friday and Saturday, June 2nd and 3rd at the Chula Vista Resort for the the DELLS RUN, June 1,2,3,4.<BR>Twin Lakes Fiero<BR>1977 E., 600 N. Rd.<BR>Paxton, Il.,  60957<BR>Ph. (217)379-9140<P>From what I've seen of the project, it is very impressive so far.||||reg||1
